---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  name="Lumi"
  tagline="is a software platform that helps businesses find and collaborate with packaging manufacturers."
  shareImage="lumi-dashboard-3"
>
  <Fragment slot="meta">
    <p><strong>Years</strong> 2019-2020</p>
    <p><strong>Role</strong> Lead Designer</p>
    <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong> Product Design, User Research</p>
    <p><strong>Collaborators</strong> 2 product managers, 1 product designer, 8 engineers</p>
    <p><strong>Platforms</strong> Web</p>
    <p class="callout">🔔 Lumi was acquired by Narvar in 2021 and sunsetted in 2024.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      Lumi is a B2B packaging and supply chain platform that connects top brands to factories around the world and
      helps with every step from sourcing to manufacturing to inventory management.
    </p>
    <p>During my time at Lumi, I touched nearly every surface of the platform during a business model transition for the company.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-unused-components', alt: 'Assorted Lumi UI components' }]} lead="Assorted UI snippets." eager>
    Some used in production and some left behind in the exploration phase.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Transitioning from Client Services to a Marketplace</h2>
    <p>
      Lumi had been building software to simplify the packaging order process between clients and vendors, but there
      was still a lot of manual intervention from Lumi staff during the quote request process.
    </p>
    <p>
      I helped bring a more structured understanding of how the workflows of clients, vendors, and internal Lumi staff
      all intersected to better understand where processes were breaking and where to maximize impact as we sought to
      retool the platform.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="figure-row">
    <Figure images={[{ name: 'FF-Member-workflow', alt: 'Managed services workflow diagram' }]} lead="Managed services workflow.">
      Lumi's team (orange row) is heavily involved in every step of the quoting and ordering process.
    </Figure>
    <Figure images={[{ name: 'FF-Marketplace-workflow', alt: 'Marketplace workflow diagram' }]} lead="Marketplace workflow.">
      New software tools would enable clients and vendors to work more closely together.
    </Figure>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Expanding Lumi's software to encompass packaging manufacturers</h2>
    <p>
      Lumi had existing software for clients and the internal quoting team, but needed to build a new portal for
      vendors to view inbound packaging requests from brands, communicate with them throughout the quoting and ordering
      process, and manage orders and shipments.
    </p>
    <p>Previous to the development of the new portal, vendors interacted with Lumi exclusively via email and PDFs.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-dashboard', alt: 'Vendor opportunities dashboard' }]} lead="Vendor opportunities.">
    A view for factories to manage inbound requests from brands and receive all of the key information they need to
    make informed business decisions.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Effectively matching clients and vendors</h2>
    <p>
      Using historic data from orders placed with Lumi's supplier network, we are able to provide clients with important
      insights about what to expect when working with a given factory. On the other side of the client/vendor
      relationship, we are also able to provide vendors with insights about clients to help facilitate a strong match on
      the platform.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-opportunity-page', alt: 'Opportunity detail view' }]} tight />
  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-quote-submitted', alt: 'Opportunity detail view after a quote is submitted' }]} lead="Opportunity detail views.">
    Vendors can see details and relevant documents about an opportunity, in addition to information about the client.
  </Figure>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'Vendor-scorecard', alt: 'Vendor quote with vendor scorecard' }]} lead="Vendor quote.">
    Clients could view pricing for a quote, plus key information about a vendor to help guide their purchase decisions.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Simplifying a convoluted ordering process</h2>
    <p>
      The world of packaging supply chain management is filled with antiquated tools and legacy systems. Lumi brought
      the digital tools used by brands and factories into the modern era of software by taking lessons from e-commerce
      to simplify the ordering experience.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-order-page', alt: 'Client order page' }]} tight />
  <Figure images={[{ name: 'lumi-vendor-order', alt: 'Vendor order page' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Lumi ID helps brands help consumers dispose of packaging sustainably</h2>
    <p>
      Lumi ID was an internal project to help provide consumers with information about their packaging and learn how to
      dispose of it properly. Lumi ID was an Honorable Mention in Fast Company's World Changing Ideas Awards in 2020.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="figure-row">
    <Figure images={[{ name: 'Lumi-ID-screenshots', alt: 'Lumi ID packaging information pages' }]} lead="Lumi ID page.">
      Consumers could scan QR codes on their packaging to see in-depth information about manufacturing, disposal, and
      more.
    </Figure>
    <Figure images={[{ name: 'Lumi-ID-QR-codes2', alt: 'Lumi ID QR code templates' }]} lead="QR code explorations.">
      Lumi provided a series of templates for brands to include in their packaging artwork that would link to the
      appropriate Lumi ID page for a piece of packaging.
    </Figure>
  </div>
</CaseStudy>
